{"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "laplace", "ucas": "laplace t^2 e^-t", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "laplace", "region_of_convergence": "Re(s) > -1", "roc": "Re(s) > -1", "one_sided": "f(t) for t >= 0 (0 before)", "rules": "e^(at) f(t) -> F(s - a), t^n f(t) -> (-1)^n F^(n)(s)", "lhs": "L{t^2*e^(-t)}(s)", "value": "2/(s + 1)^3", "headline": "L{t^2*e^(-t)}(s) = 2/(s + 1)^3"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "matches int_0^inf f(t) e^(-st) dt (Gauss-Kronrod) at s = -1/2, 1/2, 3: max relative difference 4.4e-16"}], "files": [], "text": "L{t^2*e^(-t)}(s) = 2/(s + 1)^3\n  region of convergence: Re(s) > -1\n  one-sided: f(t) for t >= 0 (0 before)\n  rules: e^(at) f(t) -> F(s - a), t^n f(t) -> (-1)^n F^(n)(s)\n  check: matches int_0^inf f(t) e^(-st) dt (Gauss-Kronrod) at s = -1/2, 1/2, 3: max relative difference 4.4e-16\n"}
{"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "ilaplace", "ucas": "ilaplace 1/(s^2 + 2s + 5)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "ilaplace", "poles": "s = -1 +- 2i", "roc": "Re(s) > -1", "lhs": "L^-1{1/(s^2 + 2s + 5)}(t)", "value": "e^(-t)*sin(2t)/2", "headline": "L^-1{1/(s^2 + 2s + 5)}(t) = e^(-t)*sin(2t)/2", "details": ["for t >= 0 (0 before): the right-sided inverse, region of convergence Re(s) > -1 (right of every pole)"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "transformed back (Gauss-Kronrod), it matches F at s = 1, 2, 7/2: max relative difference 2.2e-16"}], "files": [], "text": "L^-1{1/(s^2 + 2s + 5)}(t) = e^(-t)*sin(2t)/2\n  poles: s = -1 +- 2i\n  for t >= 0 (0 before): the right-sided inverse, region of convergence Re(s) > -1 (right of every pole)\n  check: transformed back (Gauss-Kronrod), it matches F at s = 1, 2, 7/2: max relative difference 2.2e-16\n"}
{"id": 3, "ok": true, "cmd": "laplace_solve", "ucas": "laplace solve y'' + y = sin(t), y(0) = 0, y'(0) = 1", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "laplace_solve", "transformed": "(s^2 + 1)Y(s) - 1 = 1/(s^2 + 1)", "Y(s)": "(s^2 + 2)/(s^2 + 1)^2", "y(t)": {"value": "-t*cos(t)/2 + 3sin(t)/2", "valid_for": "t >= 0"}, "poles_of_y": "+-i (double)", "headline": "y'' + y = sin(t), y(0) = 0, y'(0) = 1"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "residual of the equation at 201 points of [0, 10]: max 8.3e-16; initial values hold (max difference 0)"}, {"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "a numeric solution (RK4, h = 1/1000) agrees at 20 points of [0, 10]: max difference 1.4e-13"}], "files": [], "text": "y'' + y = sin(t), y(0) = 0, y'(0) = 1\n  transformed: (s^2 + 1)Y(s) - 1 = 1/(s^2 + 1)\n  Y(s) = (s^2 + 2)/(s^2 + 1)^2\n  y(t) = -t*cos(t)/2 + 3sin(t)/2    for t >= 0\n  poles of Y: +-i (double)\n  check: residual of the equation at 201 points of [0, 10]: max 8.3e-16; initial values hold (max difference 0)\n  check: a numeric solution (RK4, h = 1/1000) agrees at 20 points of [0, 10]: max difference 1.4e-13\n"}
{"id": 4, "ok": true, "cmd": "ztrans", "ucas": "ztrans a^n u[n]", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "ztrans", "region_of_convergence": "|z| > abs(a)", "roc": "|z| > abs(a)", "one_sided": "x[n] for n >= 0", "rules": "a^n x[n] -> X(z/a)", "lhs": "Z{a^n*u[n]}(z)", "value": "z/(z - a)", "headline": "Z{a^n*u[n]}(z) = z/(z - a)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "matches sum_n x[n] z^-n (88 terms) at z = 17/10, 17/5, 71/10 with a = 7/10: max relative difference 2e-16"}], "files": [], "text": "Z{a^n*u[n]}(z) = z/(z - a)\n  region of convergence: |z| > abs(a)\n  one-sided: x[n] for n >= 0\n  rules: a^n x[n] -> X(z/a)\n  check: matches sum_n x[n] z^-n (88 terms) at z = 17/10, 17/5, 71/10 with a = 7/10: max relative difference 2e-16\n"}
{"id": 5, "ok": true, "cmd": "iztrans", "ucas": "iztrans z/(z - 0.5)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "iztrans", "poles": "z = 1/2", "taken_as_causal_right_sided": "region of convergence |z| > 1/2", "roc": "|z| > 1/2", "long_division_in_z_1": "1, 1/2, 1/4, 1/8, 1/16, 1/32, 1/64, 1/128, ...", "lhs": "Z^-1{z/(z - 1/2)}[n]", "valid_for": "n >= 0", "value": "(1/2)^n", "headline": "Z^-1{z/(z - 1/2)}[n] = (1/2)^n    for n >= 0"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the closed form equals the long division for n = 0..31 (max difference 0)"}], "files": [], "text": "Z^-1{z/(z - 1/2)}[n] = (1/2)^n    for n >= 0\n  poles: z = 1/2\n  taken as causal (right-sided): region of convergence |z| > 1/2\n  long division in z^-1: 1, 1/2, 1/4, 1/8, 1/16, 1/32, 1/64, 1/128, ...\n  check: the closed form equals the long division for n = 0..31 (max difference 0)\n"}
{"id": 6, "ok": true, "cmd": "zsolve", "ucas": "zsolve y[n+2] = y[n+1] + y[n], y[0] = 0, y[1] = 1", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "zsolve", "transformed": "(z^2 - z - 1)Y(z) - (z) = 0", "Y(z)": "z/(z^2 - z - 1)", "y[n]": {"value": "sqrt(5)*((1 + sqrt(5))/2)^n/5 - sqrt(5)*((1 - sqrt(5))/2)^n/5", "valid_for": "n >= 0"}, "poles_of_y": "(1 + sqrt(5))/2, (1 - sqrt(5))/2", "headline": "y[n+2] = y[n+1] + y[n], y[0] = 0, y[1] = 1"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "iterating the recurrence gives the same y[0..39] (max relative difference 1.2e-15)"}], "files": [], "text": "y[n+2] = y[n+1] + y[n], y[0] = 0, y[1] = 1\n  transformed: (z^2 - z - 1)Y(z) - (z) = 0\n  Y(z) = z/(z^2 - z - 1)\n  y[n] = sqrt(5)*((1 + sqrt(5))/2)^n/5 - sqrt(5)*((1 - sqrt(5))/2)^n/5    for n >= 0\n  poles of Y: (1 + sqrt(5))/2, (1 - sqrt(5))/2\n  check: iterating the recurrence gives the same y[0..39] (max relative difference 1.2e-15)\n"}
{"id": 7, "ok": true, "cmd": "tf", "ucas": "tf y[n] = 0.9 y[n-1] + x[n]", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "tf", "input_x_output_y": "H(z) = Y(z)/X(z)", "H(z)": "10z/(10z - 9)", "value": "1/(1 - (9/10)z^-1)", "poles": "9/10", "zeros": "0", "stable_bibo": "every pole inside the unit circle (max |p| = 9/10)", "causal": "yes (deg numerator <= deg denominator)", "y1": "y;", "headline": "transfer function of y[n] = 0.9 y[n-1] + x[n] (zero initial state)", "details": ["impulse response h[n] = (9/10)^n    for n >= 0", "DC gain H(1) = 10", "frequency response H(e^(iw)), w in radians per sample:", "w          |H|          dB         phase (deg)", "0          10           20         0", "pi/8       2.60805      8.326      -63.93", "pi/4       1.36436      2.699      -60.26", "pi/2       0.743294     -2.577     -41.99", "3pi/4      0.569545     -4.889     -21.25", "pi         0.526316     -5.575     0", "-3 dB (gain 10/sqrt(2)) at w = 0.105458 rad/sample", "= 0.0167842 of the sample rate", "as C (direct form I; x1 = x[n-1], y1 = y[n-1], ...):", "float y = x + 0.9f*y1;"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "transfer function of y[n] = 0.9 y[n-1] + x[n] (zero initial state)\n  input x, output y: H(z) = Y(z)/X(z)\n  H(z) = 10z/(10z - 9)\n       = 1/(1 - (9/10)z^-1)\n  poles: 9/10\n  zeros: 0\n  stable (BIBO): every pole inside the unit circle (max |p| = 9/10)\n  causal: yes (deg numerator <= deg denominator)\n  impulse response h[n] = (9/10)^n    for n >= 0\n  DC gain H(1) = 10\n  frequency response H(e^(iw)), w in radians per sample:\n    w          |H|          dB         phase (deg)\n    0          10           20         0\n    pi/8       2.60805      8.326      -63.93\n    pi/4       1.36436      2.699      -60.26\n    pi/2       0.743294     -2.577     -41.99\n    3pi/4      0.569545     -4.889     -21.25\n    pi         0.526316     -5.575     0\n  -3 dB (gain 10/sqrt(2)) at w = 0.105458 rad/sample\n    = 0.0167842 of the sample rate\n  as C (direct form I; x1 = x[n-1], y1 = y[n-1], ...):\n    float y = x + 0.9f*y1;\n    y1 = y;\n"}
{"id": 8, "ok": true, "cmd": "fourier", "ucas": "fourier e^(-x^2)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "fourier", "convention": "F(w) = int f(x) e^(-iwx) dx over the real line (angular frequency; the inverse has 1/(2pi))", "lhs": "F{e^(-x^2)}(w)", "value": "sqrt(pi)*e^(-w^2/4)", "headline": "F{e^(-x^2)}(w) = sqrt(pi)*e^(-w^2/4)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "matches the integral computed numerically at w = 1/2, 13/10, 27/10: max relative difference 6.7e-16"}], "files": [], "text": "F{e^(-x^2)}(w) = sqrt(pi)*e^(-w^2/4)\n  convention: F(w) = int f(x) e^(-iwx) dx over the real line (angular frequency; the inverse has 1/(2pi))\n  check: matches the integral computed numerically at w = 1/2, 13/10, 27/10: max relative difference 6.7e-16\n"}
{"id": 9, "ok": true, "cmd": "fourier_series", "ucas": "fourier series x^2", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "fourier_series", "a_n": ["1/pi int f(x) cos(n*x) dx over the period, b_n likewise with sin", "4(-1)^n/n^2"], "a0": "2pi^2/3", "b_n": "0 (f is even)", "partial_sums_s_n": "||f - S_N||/||f|| = 0.0285 (N = 5), 0.0011 (N = 48)", "f_is_continuous_as_a_periodic_function": "S_N -> f uniformly (no Gibbs overshoot)", "headline": "Fourier series of x^2 on [-pi, pi] (period 2pi):", "details": ["f(x) ~ a0/2 + sum_{n>=1} a_n cos(n*x) + b_n sin(n*x)", "f(x) ~ pi^2/3 - 4cos(x) + cos(2x) - 4cos(3x)/9 + cos(4x)/4 - 4cos(5x)/25 + ..."]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the closed forms equal the numeric coefficients (Gauss-Legendre, 5120 nodes) for n = 1..48"}], "files": [], "text": "Fourier series of x^2 on [-pi, pi] (period 2pi):\n  f(x) ~ a0/2 + sum_{n>=1} a_n cos(n*x) + b_n sin(n*x)\n  a_n = 1/pi int f(x) cos(n*x) dx over the period, b_n likewise with sin\n  a0 = 2pi^2/3\n  a_n = 4(-1)^n/n^2\n  b_n = 0 (f is even)\n  check: the closed forms equal the numeric coefficients (Gauss-Legendre, 5120 nodes) for n = 1..48\n  f(x) ~ pi^2/3 - 4cos(x) + cos(2x) - 4cos(3x)/9 + cos(4x)/4 - 4cos(5x)/25 + ...\n  partial sums S_N: ||f - S_N||/||f|| = 0.0285 (N = 5), 0.0011 (N = 48)\n  f is continuous as a periodic function: S_N -> f uniformly (no Gibbs overshoot)\n"}
{"id": 10, "ok": true, "cmd": "dft", "ucas": "dft [1, 2, 3, 4]", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "dft", "n": 4, "values": [{"exact": "10", "re": 10, "im": 0, "abs": 10, "arg": 0}, {"exact": "-2 + 2i", "re": -2, "im": 2, "abs": 2.8284271247461903, "arg": 2.356194490192345}, {"exact": "-2", "re": -2, "im": 0, "abs": 2, "arg": 3.141592653589793}, {"exact": "-2 - 2i", "re": -1.9999999999999998, "im": -2, "abs": 2.82842712474619, "arg": -2.356194490192345}], "headline": "DFT of 4 values (X[k] = sum_n x[n] e^(-2 pi i k n/N); radix-2 FFT, N log2 N operations)", "details": ["k    X[k]                         |.|            arg", "0    10                           10             0", "1    -2 + 2i                      2sqrt(2)       3pi/4", "2    -2                           2              pi", "3    -2 - 2i                      2sqrt(2)       -3pi/4", "bin k is the frequency k/N cycles per sample; k > N/2 are the negative frequencies k - N"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the inverse transform gives the input back (max difference 0); Parseval: sum |x|^2 = 30, sum |X|^2/N = 30"}], "files": [], "text": "DFT of 4 values (X[k] = sum_n x[n] e^(-2 pi i k n/N); radix-2 FFT, N log2 N operations)\n  k    X[k]                         |.|            arg\n  0    10                           10             0\n  1    -2 + 2i                      2sqrt(2)       3pi/4\n  2    -2                           2              pi\n  3    -2 - 2i                      2sqrt(2)       -3pi/4\n  check: the inverse transform gives the input back (max difference 0); Parseval: sum |x|^2 = 30, sum |X|^2/N = 30\n  bin k is the frequency k/N cycles per sample; k > N/2 are the negative frequencies k - N\n"}
